1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,851
In this walkthrough, you'll turn a Figma design

2
00:00:02,851 --> 00:00:05,001
into a clickable app prototype with Claude.

3
00:00:05,281 --> 00:00:07,903
Then you'll put it online with GitHub Pages and

4
00:00:07,903 --> 00:00:09,911
test it with real people on a phone.

5
00:00:10,191 --> 00:00:11,940
You don't need to write any code.

6
00:00:13,333 --> 00:00:15,296
Step one is a one-off setup.

7
00:00:15,576 --> 00:00:18,093
In your web browser, go to claude dot A I.

8
00:00:18,373 --> 00:00:19,888
The free plan is fine.

9
00:00:20,168 --> 00:00:23,283
Open Customize, then Connectors, and browse for Figma.

10
00:00:23,563 --> 00:00:26,443
Click Connect, sign in to Figma, and approve access.

11
00:00:26,723 --> 00:00:28,609
Then start a new chat and check that

12
00:00:28,609 --> 00:00:30,861
Figma is switched on under the plus button.

13
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:34,303
Next, get your Figma page ready.

14
00:00:34,583 --> 00:00:37,764
Put every screen on one page, as separate frames, and give

15
00:00:37,764 --> 00:00:40,343
each frame a clear name, like Sign in, or Home.

16
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:43,311
Claude uses these names to tell the screens apart.

17
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,663
Select everything on the canvas.

18
00:00:46,943 --> 00:00:49,324
Then, in the left panel, right-click the page

19
00:00:49,324 --> 00:00:51,124
name and choose Copy link to page.

20
00:00:51,404 --> 00:00:54,753
A link to the whole page lets Claude see every screen at once.

21
00:00:56,133 --> 00:00:58,301
Paste the link into Claude, and ask it

22
00:00:58,301 --> 00:01:01,211
to build every screen into one clickable prototype.

23
00:01:01,491 --> 00:01:04,374
Claude reads the page through the Figma connector, pulling

24
00:01:04,374 --> 00:01:06,760
in the layout, colours and text for each screen.

25
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:09,067
You don't need to do anything while it works.

26
00:01:10,433 --> 00:01:13,228
The prototype opens in a panel beside the chat.

27
00:01:13,508 --> 00:01:16,089
Click through it and compare each screen with Figma.

28
00:01:16,369 --> 00:01:20,257
Photos and illustrations may be simplified, and any typos in your

29
00:01:20,257 --> 00:01:23,367
design get copied across, so ask Claude to fix them.

30
00:01:24,733 --> 00:01:27,133
To save it, click the small arrow next

31
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:29,469
to Copy, and choose Download as HTML.

32
00:01:29,749 --> 00:01:32,203
That single file is the whole prototype.

33
00:01:33,567 --> 00:01:36,617
To test on phones, the prototype needs a web address.

34
00:01:36,897 --> 00:01:40,677
Upload the file to a GitHub repository, rename it index

35
00:01:40,677 --> 00:01:43,425
dot H T M L, and switch on GitHub Pages.

36
00:01:43,705 --> 00:01:46,607
You'll get a github dot I O link to use for testing.

37
00:01:46,887 --> 00:01:50,108
Other tutorials take you through setting up GitHub Pages.

38
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:53,975
Now tell Claude what your participants will do.

39
00:01:54,255 --> 00:01:56,388
In this project there are three tasks:

40
00:01:56,668 --> 00:01:59,714
check the account balance, transfer a hundred and fifty

41
00:01:59,714 --> 00:02:02,151
pounds to Harper, and pay the electric bill.

42
00:02:02,431 --> 00:02:05,524
You can also ask Claude to set up how the sign-in behaves.

43
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:09,055
It's a phone app, so test it on a phone.

44
00:02:09,335 --> 00:02:13,559
Scan the QR code to open the prototype, and check it fills the screen.

45
00:02:13,839 --> 00:02:17,337
Then tap Full screen in the bottom corner to hide the browser bars.

46
00:02:17,617 --> 00:02:21,095
On an iPhone, Safari may not allow full screen, and that's fine.

47
00:02:22,467 --> 00:02:25,539
Before the session, download the documents from the repository.

48
00:02:25,819 --> 00:02:29,339
Each participant reads and signs the informed consent form.

49
00:02:29,619 --> 00:02:32,736
The facilitator guide takes you through the session, and there's

50
00:02:32,736 --> 00:02:35,123
a checklist and quick prompts to keep beside you.

51
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:37,844
Now run the test.

52
00:02:38,124 --> 00:02:41,153
Get signed consent, and follow the facilitator guide.

53
00:02:41,433 --> 00:02:45,231
Refresh the page before each participant, so they start at Sign in.

54
00:02:45,511 --> 00:02:49,329
Read each task aloud, ask them to think aloud, and note what you see.

55
00:02:49,609 --> 00:02:53,343
The prototype accepts any amount, so check their answers yourself.

56
00:02:54,733 --> 00:02:58,595
If something isn't right, just ask Claude for a change in plain words.

57
00:02:58,875 --> 00:03:02,181
For example, fix a typo, or add a screen for the water bill.

58
00:03:03,567 --> 00:03:04,847
So, to recap:

59
00:03:05,127 --> 00:03:09,399
connect Claude to Figma, copy the page link, build the prototype, download

60
00:03:09,399 --> 00:03:12,401
it, host it on GitHub Pages, and test it on a phone.

61
00:03:12,681 --> 00:03:14,260
Good luck with your testing.
